.TH SOVEREIGN-MESH 7 "May 2026" "v1.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
sovereign-mesh \- Swarm consensus and 7-layer pedigree architecture
.SH DESCRIPTION
The **Sovereign Mesh** employs a collective intelligence model governed by a strict 7-layer relational pedigree and a majority-based consensus engine.
.SH 7-LAYER PEDIGREE ARCHITECTURE
Agents inherit specialties and permissions tracing back to \fBAGENT-0\fR.
.TP
\fBLayer 1: Core Swarm Mind\fR
Root progenitor swarm mind (\fBAGENT-0\fR).
.TP
\fBLayer 2: Domain Sovereignty\fR
Security, Telemetry, and Execution Overlords.
.TP
\fBLayer 3: Functional Specialization\fR
Modules for Auth, Process, and Network migration.
.TP
\fBLayer 6: Shared Resource Bindings\fR
Hardware allocations and IPC Shared Memory mappings (\fBAGENT-MMAP\fR).
.TP
\fBLayer 7: Execution Interfaces\fR
gRPC instances and bidirectional dialect nodes.
.SH SWARM CONSENSUS MECHANICS
State mutations require a **4/5 majority consensus** from the Consensus Evaluation Panel:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAGENT-SEC\fR (Security Overlord)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAGENT-TEL\fR (Telemetry Watcher)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAGENT-EXEC\fR (Execution Spawner)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAGENT-AUTH\fR (Auth Specialist)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAGENT-MIG\fR (Migrator Engine)
.SH MINORITY REPORTS
Mutations with dissent (e.g., 4/5 agreement) trigger a \fBMinority Report Cause-Effect Research Analysis\fR. This forensic process evaluates operational risk and boundary deviances, ensuring full transparency in the ledger.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBstarbirth\fR(7), \fBjetweb\fR(7), \fBsovereign-cli\fR(1)
